  "articleBody": "It's a common question, and a good one, when you're planning a natural stone tile project. You don't want to run out mid-job, but you also don't want a ton of waste. The general rule of thumb is to order about 10–15% extra. This isn't just for mishaps during installation, like a tile breaking while being cut. It also accounts for future repairs. Imagine you have a plumbing leak down the line and need to replace a few tiles; having those spares on hand will save you a lot of headache trying to find a matching lot. Plus, natural stone has variations, so that extra bit helps ensure a consistent look. Always keep those factors in mind when you're planning your purchase. If you're unsure, it's always best to chat with your installer. We're happy to guide you through the process, making sure you get just what you need without going overboard. Getting it right from the start makes everything go smoother.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}